/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (Path traversal vulnerabilities are a type of security flaw that allows an attacker to access files and directories stored outside the intended directory on a web server. This vulnerability occurs when an application uses unvalidated user input to construct file paths, which might be later used to read a file. Attackers can exploit this by manipulating the file paths to gain unauthorized access to sensitive files or directories, potentially leading to access of file system, which can potentially result in data breaches or system compromise.)
